  "prefLabel": "Res 2704.09 Deadline for Submitting Applications",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 2704.09 Deadline for Submitting Applications. An eligible business shall submit its application at least two weeks prior to a committee meeting. Late applications shall be considered by the committee if good cause for failing to meet the deadline exists. Good cause shall include, but not be limited to, loss of information due to fire, theft or other circumstances beyond the control of the business. Claims of good cause shall be made in writing to the committee and the commissioner.\n\nSource. #8975, INTERIM, eff 9-14-07, EXPIRED: 3-12-08\n\nNew. #9498, eff 7-1-09 (from Res 2704.08), EXPIRED: 7-1-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res2700.html"
